Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese Trainer Hill
Applies after 0061-japanese-built-text.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The Japanese ROM's Trainer Hill has no modes: the attendant starts its one challenge
of two floors (the decomp's JP default, whose data equals that ROM's but for the
trainer record layout) without asking for a tag match type, and the challenge id
in the save keeps a single best time. Its time board lists each floor's trainers
under the clear time. The port maps the two floors' mazes as arrays, as it does
the international ones. Other languages are unchanged.

